  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sumatran Tiger Conservation in Ulu Masen, Indonesia, Island Wide Survey Assessment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Leuser-Ulu Masen Landscape in Aceh province, Indonesia, represents a very important forest habitat for the Critically Endangered Sumatran tiger. From 2007-2009, the first ever robust Sumatra-Wide detection/non-detection Tiger Survey (SWTS) following the patch occupancy framework was conducted to estimate the proportion of area occupied by the Critically Endangered Sumatran tiger. After ten years, there is an urgent requirement to reassess the island-wide population to evaluate the implementation of past conservation strategies in different landscapes, including Ulu Masen. The survey result will help the Government of Indonesia and also the Government of Aceh to meet its ambitious National Tiger Recovery Plan (NTRP) target of doubling the number of Sumatran tigers by 2022. This proposal will enable FFI to contribute the Ulu Masen portion of the island-wide survey. Project objectives are: (1) To increase the capacity of government officers on tiger site occupancy in Ulu Masen; and, (2) To conduct and analyze occupancy survey in Ulu Masen landscape.</narrative>
  </description>
